-- int-tests-fixtures.l4: the named cases that the integration tests share. No assertion lives here. GENERATED by work/integrator/gen_fixtures.py from the DECLAREs of the group modules.
-- A record of the Law has no update operator, so each case is a full literal; in a 'clear' case every BOOLEAN is FALSE, every MAYBE NOTHING and every LIST empty unless the name says otherwise.
-- A case is named for its FACTS, never for the answer it is expected to give.

§ `Integration layer -- the cases the tests share`

§§ `A body, described by the statements that are true of it`

DECLARE `A thing true of a body in the case` IS ONE OF
    `it is the trustees of a trust`
    `it is the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`
    `it is a body corporate`
    `it is an NPO`
    `it is established under the law of Jersey`
    `it is an incorporated 1862 association`
    `it is a foundation`
    `it was established by an enactment`
    `it was established by Act of the States`
    `it was established by Royal Charter`
    `it was established in relation to Jersey`
    `it is a company`
    `it is incorporated under, but not by, an enactment`
    `it is incorporated under, but not by, a UK Act`
    `it is an unincorporated body`
    `it is a partnership`
    `it is established under the law of another jurisdiction`
    `its relationship is governed by the law of Jersey`

GIVEN true IS A LIST OF `A thing true of a body in the case` @desc The statements that are true of the body
      governors IS A LIST OF Governor @desc The governors the facts list
GIVETH A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
`Int fx a body with` true governors MEANS
    `Facts about the body under Article 2` WITH
        `the person or persons, taken together, who are the trustees of a trust` IS elem `it is the trustees of a trust` true
        `the person or persons, taken together, who are the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` IS elem `it is the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` true
        `a body corporate` IS elem `it is a body corporate` true
        `an NPO, as defined by the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008` IS elem `it is an NPO` true
        `established under the law of Jersey` IS elem `it is established under the law of Jersey` true
        `an association incorporated under Article 4 of the Loi of 1862` IS elem `it is an incorporated 1862 association` true
        `a foundation under the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009` IS elem `it is a foundation` true
        `established by an enactment` IS elem `it was established by an enactment` true
        `established by Act of the States` IS elem `it was established by Act of the States` true
        `established by Royal Charter` IS elem `it was established by Royal Charter` true
        `established in relation to Jersey` IS elem `it was established in relation to Jersey` true
        `the Law by which the body corporate was established` IS NOTHING
        `a company under the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` IS elem `it is a company` true
        `incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` IS elem `it is incorporated under, but not by, an enactment` true
        `incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council, as such Act or Order is extended to or applicable in Jersey` IS elem `it is incorporated under, but not by, a UK Act` true
        `the enactment under which the body was incorporated` IS NOTHING
        `the persons, taken together, who constitute for the time being an unincorporated body or association of persons` IS elem `it is an unincorporated body` true
        `a partnership` IS elem `it is a partnership` true
        `the kinds mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a) to (h) that the body is substantially similar to` IS EMPTY
        `established under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey` IS elem `it is established under the law of another jurisdiction` true
        `the law governing the relationship between the persons constituting it, in that capacity, is the law of Jersey` IS elem `its relationship is governed by the law of Jersey` true
        `the sub-paragraphs added by Order within which the body falls` IS EMPTY
        governors IS governors

-- A company established in Jersey: kind (f), a Jersey entity by Article 2(3)(a).
GIVEN governors IS A LIST OF Governor @desc The governors
GIVETH A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
`Int fx a Jersey company` governors MEANS
    `Int fx a body with` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it is a company`, `it is established under the law of Jersey`) governors

-- An unincorporated association governed by the law of Jersey: kind (i), a Jersey entity by Article 2(3)(b) only if a governor qualifies.
GIVEN governors IS A LIST OF Governor @desc The governors
GIVETH A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
`Int fx a Jersey unincorporated association` governors MEANS
    `Int fx a body with` (LIST `it is an unincorporated body`, `its relationship is governed by the law of Jersey`) governors

-- A body corporate established under the law of another jurisdiction: kind (j) only if it is substantially similar to one of (a) to (h), which is an input.
GIVEN similar IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity` @desc The sub-paragraphs among (a) to (h) that the body is substantially similar to
GIVETH A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
`Int fx a foreign body similar to` similar MEANS
    `Facts about the body under Article 2` WITH
        `the person or persons, taken together, who are the trustees of a trust` IS FALSE
        `the person or persons, taken together, who are the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis` IS FALSE
        `a body corporate` IS TRUE
        `an NPO, as defined by the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008` IS FALSE
        `established under the law of Jersey` IS FALSE
        `an association incorporated under Article 4 of the Loi of 1862` IS FALSE
        `a foundation under the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009` IS FALSE
        `established by an enactment` IS FALSE
        `established by Act of the States` IS FALSE
        `established by Royal Charter` IS FALSE
        `established in relation to Jersey` IS FALSE
        `the Law by which the body corporate was established` IS NOTHING
        `a company under the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` IS FALSE
        `incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991` IS FALSE
        `incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council, as such Act or Order is extended to or applicable in Jersey` IS FALSE
        `the enactment under which the body was incorporated` IS NOTHING
        `the persons, taken together, who constitute for the time being an unincorporated body or association of persons` IS FALSE
        `a partnership` IS FALSE
        `the kinds mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a) to (h) that the body is substantially similar to` IS similar
        `established under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey` IS TRUE
        `the law governing the relationship between the persons constituting it, in that capacity, is the law of Jersey` IS FALSE
        `the sub-paragraphs added by Order within which the body falls` IS EMPTY
        `governors` IS EMPTY

-- An NPO body corporate established under the law of Jersey that is none of (c) to (h): sub-paragraph (ba), from the text of 16 October 2025.
GIVETH A `Facts about the body under Article 2`
`Int fx an NPO body corporate` MEANS
    `Int fx a body with` (LIST `it is a body corporate`, `it is an NPO`, `it is established under the law of Jersey`) EMPTY

§§ `The people`

GIVEN name IS A STRING @desc The name
GIVETH A Governor
`Int fx a natural person resident in Jersey called` name MEANS
    Governor WITH name IS name, `is a natural person` IS TRUE, `is resident in Jersey` IS TRUE, `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS FALSE, `reportable matters` IS EMPTY

GIVEN name IS A STRING @desc The name
GIVETH A Governor
`Int fx a natural person resident abroad called` name MEANS
    Governor WITH name IS name, `is a natural person` IS TRUE, `is resident in Jersey` IS FALSE, `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS FALSE, `reportable matters` IS EMPTY

-- The role of a director of the company.
GIVETH A `Facts about a person's role in an entity`
`Int fx a director` MEANS
    `Facts about a person's role in an entity` WITH
        `a trustee of the trust or a fidéicommissaire of the fidéicommis` IS FALSE
        `a member of the council of the foundation` IS FALSE
        `a director of the company` IS TRUE
        `a member of the management committee of the entity` IS FALSE
        `relation to the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` IS `holds the general control and management as one of a number of governors`

-- The role of a person who has no role in the body.
GIVETH A `Facts about a person's role in an entity`
`Int fx a stranger` MEANS
    `Facts about a person's role in an entity` WITH
        `a trustee of the trust or a fidéicommissaire of the fidéicommis` IS FALSE
        `a member of the council of the foundation` IS FALSE
        `a director of the company` IS FALSE
        `a member of the management committee of the entity` IS FALSE
        `relation to the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` IS `holds none of the general control and management`

GIVEN name IS A STRING @desc The name
GIVETH A `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)`
`Int fx the clear conduct of` name MEANS
    `Conduct of a governor for Article 18(4)` WITH
        `name` IS name
        `the conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)` IS FALSE
        `concurs in the misconduct of the charity` IS FALSE
        `assists or encourages these other governors to engage in misconduct` IS EMPTY
        `becomes aware or ought to have become aware of misconduct, or of the intention of another governor to engage in it` IS FALSE
        `actively conceals that misconduct or that intention` IS FALSE
        `continues the concealment beyond a reasonable time` IS FALSE
        `fails within a reasonable time to take proper steps to protect or restore the property of the charity or to prevent the misconduct` IS FALSE

GIVEN name IS A STRING @desc The name
GIVETH A `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)`
`Int fx the clear facts for the reportable matters of` name MEANS
    `Facts about a person for Article 19(1)` WITH
        `conduct as a governor` IS `Int fx the clear conduct of` name
        `the governors of the charity` IS EMPTY
        `the conduct of the charity is misconduct within Article 2(10)` IS FALSE
        `the misconduct led to the service of a required steps notice` IS FALSE
        `disqualification orders under this Law` IS EMPTY
        `subject to another restriction on acting as a governor under this Law` IS FALSE
        `disqualifications as a charity trustee or an equivalent` IS EMPTY
        `disqualifications as a company director or an equivalent outside Jersey` IS EMPTY
        `bankrupt or otherwise insolvent` IS FALSE
        `convictions` IS EMPTY
        `falls within another description prescribed by Order` IS FALSE

-- A director who is a governor, with nothing to report and a declaration of no reportable matter.
GIVEN name IS A STRING @desc The name
GIVETH A `Person in the case`
`Int fx a director with nothing to report called` name MEANS
    `Person in the case` WITH
        considered IS `Person considered as a governor` WITH person IS `Int fx a natural person resident in Jersey called` name, role IS `Int fx a director`
        `facts for the reportable matters` IS `Int fx the clear facts for the reportable matters of` name
        `made a report under paragraph (2)` IS FALSE
        `provided a declaration of no reportable matter` IS TRUE
        `reported matter awaiting determination` IS NOTHING

§§ `Purposes and the charity test`

GIVEN description IS A STRING @desc The purpose in words
      head IS A `Head of charitable purpose` @desc The head of Article 6(1) it falls under
GIVETH A Purpose
`Int fx a charitable purpose` description head MEANS
    Purpose WITH description IS description, head IS JUST head, `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE, `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE, `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE

GIVETH A Purpose
`Int fx a political party purpose` MEANS
    Purpose WITH description IS "to advance a political party", head IS NOTHING, `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE, `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS TRUE, `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE

GIVEN purpose IS A Purpose @desc The purpose
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` purpose MEANS
    `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads` WITH purpose IS purpose, facts IS (`Facts about a purpose under Article 6` WITH
            `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS FALSE
            `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS FALSE
            `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS FALSE
            `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS NOTHING
            `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS NOTHING
            `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS NOTHING
            `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE
            `the purpose promotes equality` IS NOTHING
            `the purpose promotes diversity` IS NOTHING
            `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS NOTHING
            `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE)

GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`Int fx a constitution with no permission` MEANS
    `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)` WITH `permissions that the constitution expressly makes` IS EMPTY

-- A determination by the Commissioner that the entity provides public benefit, made in compliance with the duties of Article 7.
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`Int fx a determination that public benefit is provided` MEANS
    `Determination of public benefit` WITH
        `who made the determination` IS `the Commissioner`
        `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS TRUE
        `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS TRUE
        `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS TRUE
        `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE
        `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS TRUE
        `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE
        `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS FALSE
        `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS FALSE

GIVEN determination IS A `Determination of public benefit` @desc The determination
GIVETH A `Facts for the charity test in the case`
`Int fx the charity test facts with` determination MEANS
    `Facts for the charity test in the case` WITH `constitution facts` IS `Int fx a constitution with no permission`, `public benefit determination` IS determination, `an Order under Article 5(3) disapplies Article 5(2) for the entity` IS FALSE

§§ `The application`

-- All the information the application must include, provided; no Order disapplies any provision; no payment to a governor in the twelve months.
GIVEN lodged IS A DATE @desc The day the application was lodged
GIVETH AN `Application for registration`
`Int fx a complete application lodged on` lodged MEANS
    `Application for registration` WITH
        dates IS `Dates of an application` WITH `date lodged` IS lodged, `date on which it became complete` IS JUST lodged
        `particulars under Article 11(2)(a)` IS `Particulars under Article 11(2)(a)` WITH
            `how the applicant meets Article 11(4)(c) and (d)` IS `Information on a matter under Article 11(2)(a)` WITH `provided as at the time of the application` IS TRUE, `would differ once the entity is registered` IS FALSE, `provided as proposed once the entity is registered` IS FALSE
            `matters under Article 8(3)(a), (b) and (d)` IS `Information on a matter under Article 11(2)(a)` WITH `provided as at the time of the application` IS TRUE, `would differ once the entity is registered` IS FALSE, `provided as proposed once the entity is registered` IS FALSE
            `matters under Article 8(3)(h), (i), (m) and (n) apply to the applicant` IS FALSE
            `matters under Article 8(3)(h), (i), (m) and (n)` IS `Information on a matter under Article 11(2)(a)` WITH `provided as at the time of the application` IS TRUE, `would differ once the entity is registered` IS FALSE, `provided as proposed once the entity is registered` IS FALSE
        `documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)` IS `Documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)` WITH `copy of the applicant's constitution` IS TRUE, `draft of the proposed statement of registered charitable purposes` IS TRUE, `draft of the registered public benefit statement` IS TRUE
        `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)` IS `Financial details under Article 11(2)(e)` WITH
            `most recent financial accounts exist` IS TRUE
            `details of the most recent financial accounts` IS TRUE
            `payments made to governors` IS EMPTY
            `payments to governors disclosed in the application` IS EMPTY
            `draft of the proposed statement under an Order under Article 13(9)(b)` IS FALSE
            `Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008 would require other financial information` IS FALSE
            `other financial information required under that Law` IS FALSE
            `entry in the restricted section is requested` IS FALSE
            `Order prescribes further financial information` IS FALSE
            `further financial information prescribed by Order` IS FALSE
        `other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)` IS `Other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)` WITH
            `Regulations under Article 11(3) require other information, documents or evidence` IS FALSE
            `other information, documents and evidence required by Regulations` IS FALSE
            `procedure under Regulations under Article 11(3)(b) followed` IS TRUE
            `Commissioner has requested other information, documents or evidence to determine the application` IS FALSE
            `other information, documents and evidence requested by the Commissioner` IS FALSE
        `provisions of Article 11(2) that an Order disapplies for this applicant` IS EMPTY

-- The same application with the copy of the constitution missing (Article 11(2)(b)).
GIVEN lodged IS A DATE @desc The day the application was lodged
GIVETH AN `Application for registration`
`Int fx an application lodged on without a copy of the constitution` lodged MEANS
    `Application for registration` WITH
        dates IS `Dates of an application` WITH `date lodged` IS lodged, `date on which it became complete` IS NOTHING
        `particulars under Article 11(2)(a)` IS (`Int fx a complete application lodged on` lodged)'s `particulars under Article 11(2)(a)`
        `documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)` IS `Documents under Article 11(2)(b) to (d)` WITH `copy of the applicant's constitution` IS FALSE, `draft of the proposed statement of registered charitable purposes` IS TRUE, `draft of the registered public benefit statement` IS TRUE
        `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)` IS (`Int fx a complete application lodged on` lodged)'s `financial details under Article 11(2)(e)`
        `other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)` IS (`Int fx a complete application lodged on` lodged)'s `other requirements under Article 11(2)(f)`
        `provisions of Article 11(2) that an Order disapplies for this applicant` IS EMPTY

-- The Commissioner's findings when nothing is amiss: the applicant meets the charity test now (so there is no finding that it WILL meet it on registration), its constitution is written, it carries out a substantial activity in Jersey, and no ground prescribed under Article 11(7) applies.
GIVETH A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)`
`Int fx clear findings` MEANS
    `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)` WITH
        `applicant will meet the charity test on registration` IS FALSE
        `constitution of the applicant is a written document` IS TRUE
        `applicant carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey` IS TRUE
        `activity is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial` IS TRUE
        `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application must be refused applies` IS FALSE
        `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application may be refused has its circumstances present` IS FALSE
        `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application may be refused should be applied` IS FALSE

-- A foreign applicant with no activity in Jersey.
GIVETH A `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)`
`Int fx findings with no activity in Jersey` MEANS
    `Findings of the Commissioner for Article 11(4)` WITH
        `applicant will meet the charity test on registration` IS FALSE
        `constitution of the applicant is a written document` IS TRUE
        `applicant carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey` IS FALSE
        `activity is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial` IS FALSE
        `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application must be refused applies` IS FALSE
        `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application may be refused has its circumstances present` IS FALSE
        `a ground prescribed under Article 11(7) on which the application may be refused should be applied` IS FALSE

GIVEN name IS A STRING @desc The proposed registered name
GIVETH AN `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name`
`Int fx a name with no objection` name MEANS
    `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` WITH
        `name in question` IS name
        `entries in the register that are the same as, or too similar to, the name` IS EMPTY
        `likely to mislead the public as to the purpose, activities or identity of the entity` IS FALSE
        `gives the impression that the entity is connected to a person to which it is not connected` IS FALSE
        `offensive` IS FALSE

GIVEN name IS A STRING @desc The proposed registered name
      other IS A `Name entered in the register` @desc The entry of another charity that is too similar
GIVETH AN `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name`
`Int fx a name too similar to` name other MEANS
    `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` WITH
        `name in question` IS name
        `entries in the register that are the same as, or too similar to, the name` IS LIST other
        `likely to mislead the public as to the purpose, activities or identity of the entity` IS FALSE
        `gives the impression that the entity is connected to a person to which it is not connected` IS FALSE
        `offensive` IS FALSE

GIVEN name IS A STRING @desc The name
GIVETH A `Name entered in the register`
`Int fx the registered name of another charity` name MEANS
    `Name entered in the register` WITH name IS name, `kind of entry` IS `the registered name`, `standing of the entity that holds it` IS `entered in the general section`, `held by the entity itself` IS FALSE

-- Registered office in Jersey: Article 8(4)(a) applies to a company whose constitutional Law requires one.
GIVEN address IS A STRING @desc The registered office
GIVETH A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))`
`Int fx a registered office in Jersey at` address MEANS
    `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` WITH
        `its constitutional Law requires a registered office or business address in Jersey` IS TRUE
        `registered office or business address in Jersey` IS JUST address
        `main premises in Jersey from which its activities in Jersey are managed, controlled or undertaken` IS NOTHING
        `addresses in Jersey of the governors` IS EMPTY

GIVETH A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))`
`Int fx no address in Jersey` MEANS
    `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` WITH
        `its constitutional Law requires a registered office or business address in Jersey` IS FALSE
        `registered office or business address in Jersey` IS NOTHING
        `main premises in Jersey from which its activities in Jersey are managed, controlled or undertaken` IS NOTHING
        `addresses in Jersey of the governors` IS EMPTY

-- The model constitution of Article 2(8): none conforming.
GIVETH A `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)`
`Int fx clear model facts` MEANS
    `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)` WITH
        `the constitution conforms to the model` IS FALSE
        `published by the Commissioner` IS `Facts about a publication` WITH `made available by the person in some manner` IS FALSE, `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS FALSE, `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS FALSE
        `published for the purpose of Article 2(8)` IS FALSE
        `the model provides for the entity to have a management committee` IS FALSE

-- A reported matter that the governor has reported to the Commissioner and that is not yet determined (Article 19(9)(c) then bars granting an application).
GIVETH A `Reported matter under Article 19(9)`
`Int fx a reported matter not yet determined` MEANS
    `Reported matter under Article 19(9)` WITH
        `the governor reported the matter to the Commissioner` IS TRUE
        `the Commissioner has applied to the court to determine the issue` IS FALSE
        `the issue has been determined` IS FALSE
        `any resulting order or notice has been complied with` IS FALSE

-- A reported matter that has been determined and whose resulting order has been complied with (Article 19(9)(c) no longer bars).
GIVETH A `Reported matter under Article 19(9)`
`Int fx a reported matter determined and complied with` MEANS
    `Reported matter under Article 19(9)` WITH
        `the governor reported the matter to the Commissioner` IS TRUE
        `the Commissioner has applied to the court to determine the issue` IS FALSE
        `the issue has been determined` IS TRUE
        `any resulting order or notice has been complied with` IS TRUE

§§ `The register`

GIVEN address IS A STRING @desc The principal address entered
GIVETH A `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)`
`Int fx clear facts for the items of Article 8(3) with the address` address MEANS
    `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)` WITH
        `other premises` IS EMPTY
        `principal address entered` IS JUST address
        `previous registered names` IS EMPTY
        `information prescribed by an Order under Article 8(3)(n)` IS EMPTY

GIVEN section IS A `Section of the register` @desc The section
      date IS A DATE @desc The date of the entry
GIVETH A `Placement of an entity in a section of the register`
`Int fx a placement in` section date MEANS
    `Placement of an entity in a section of the register` WITH `the section` IS section, `date of the entry` IS date

GIVEN placements IS A LIST OF `Placement of an entity in a section of the register` @desc The placements before deregistration
GIVETH A `Facts for the items of Article 8(5)`
`Int fx facts for the items of Article 8(5) with the placements` placements MEANS
    `Facts for the items of Article 8(5)` WITH
        `placements of the entity before deregistration` IS placements
        `previous registered names` IS EMPTY
        `matters prescribed by an Order under Article 8(5)(e)` IS EMPTY

GIVETH A `Facts for the public elements (Article 9(1))`
`Int fx facts for the public elements with a summary of reasons` MEANS
    `Facts for the public elements (Article 9(1))` WITH
        `a summary of the reasons has been produced by the charity to the satisfaction of the Commissioner` IS TRUE
        `an Order under Article 9(1)(d) prescribes another element` IS FALSE

GIVETH AN `Order under Article 28 as it applies to a charity`
`Int fx no Order under Article 28` MEANS
    `Order under Article 28 as it applies to a charity` WITH
        `the Order categorizes the charity as an organized religious charity` IS FALSE
        `the Order gives the Commissioner discretion to grant or withdraw the status` IS FALSE
        `the Commissioner has granted the status` IS FALSE
        `the Commissioner has withdrawn the status` IS FALSE

GIVETH AN `Order under Article 28 as it applies to a charity`
`Int fx an Order under Article 28 categorizing the charity` MEANS
    `Order under Article 28 as it applies to a charity` WITH
        `the Order categorizes the charity as an organized religious charity` IS TRUE
        `the Order gives the Commissioner discretion to grant or withdraw the status` IS FALSE
        `the Commissioner has granted the status` IS FALSE
        `the Commissioner has withdrawn the status` IS FALSE

-- A permission that a constitution expressly makes for a Minister (not 'the Minister' of Article 1) to direct or control the activities of the entity, in that capacity: Article 5(2)(a).
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
